---
title: Vector Theme not available for current version of MediaWiki
date: 2010-06-16
topics: MediaWiki
---

You may have noticed
[Wikipedia](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Harbors,_Minnesota) has [a new
interface](http://blog.wikimedia.org/2010/wikimedia-gets-ready-for-some-big-changes/)
these days. If you run your own
[MediaWiki](http://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/MediaWiki) website, the obvious
question in your mind is, how can I get these improvements on my site too?

This information is surprisingly hard to find, but the short answer is: you
can’t yet.

> ***How can I use Wikipedia’s new skin (Vector) on my wiki?***
>
> Vector is not available in MediaWiki versions prior to 1.16, and will be made
> default skin in 1.17.

—buried in the [MediaWiki
FAQ](http://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/FAQ#How_can_I_use_Wikipedia.27s_new_skin_.28Vector.29_on_my_wiki.3F)

As of the time of this writing (June 2010), 1.16 is still in beta, and 1.17 has
no planned release date. Check the [MediaWiki version
lifecycle](http://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Version_lifecycle) for current
information.
